# cleura_openstack_user (Resource)

Manages an **OpenStack user** (a Keystone user) in your Cleura account. OpenStack users
authenticate against OpenStack itself — with the OpenStack CLI, `clouds.yaml`, or the
OpenStack Terraform provider — and are typically used for automation and service accounts.
They are **distinct from Cleura account users**, who log in to the Cleura Cloud control
panel and this API.

Users live in an **OpenStack domain**. By default the provider uses the domain that serves
its configured `region`; set `domain_id` when the account has several domains for the region
(list them with `cleura openstack domain list`). `domain_id` cannot change after creation.

`name`, `description`, `enabled`, and the password are updated **in place**. Destroying the
resource deletes the user.

-> **Domains:** the domain this resource lives in is derived from the provider's `region`; see
[OpenStack projects, users and domains](../guides/openstack-identity.md) for how that works and
when to set `domain_id`.

## Password handling

`password` is a **write-only** argument (Terraform 1.11 or later): it is sent to the API on
create but is never stored in state or shown in plans. Because Terraform cannot see it, it
also cannot tell when it changes. To rotate the password, change `password` **and** bump
`password_wo_version` (any string, for example `"2"`); the next apply re-sends the current
`password`. Edits to other attributes never touch the password.

## Project access

A new user has **no access to any project**. Grant it roles on projects with the
[`cleura_openstack_role_assignment`](openstack_role_assignment.md) resource:

```terraform
resource "cleura_openstack_role_assignment" "ci" {
  user_id    = cleura_openstack_user.ci.id
  project_id = cleura_openstack_project.example.id
  roles      = ["member"]
}
```

### Prerequisites

The provider must be authenticated and have a `region`. `project_id` is **not** required:
this resource is account-scoped. See the provider's
[Authentication](../index.md#authentication) documentation.

